� ��ų'5�mDt!�R��{�?`�uf�`簻x�����I��:A�E�W%&���T@0H��.Z���Դ��R�4d�"r�!�ڔ�fe�����#��q�`b�$�<���b�x␀␀��B�6�D�Sk␀␀␀��␀.����f␀,7:headers;1679:40:4:Date,29:Mon, 06 Apr 2026 14:05:56 GMT,]52:12:Content-Type,32:text/event-stream; charset=utf-8,]31:17:Transfer-Encoding,7:chunked,]28:10:Connection,10:keep-alive,]28:13:Cache-Control,8:no-cache,]52:38:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-limit,7:2000000,]56:42:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-remaining,7:1994000,]66:38:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T14:05:56Z,]52:39:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-limit,6:400000,]56:43:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-remaining,6:400000,]67:39:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T14:05:55Z,]45:34:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-limit,4:4000,]49:38:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-remaining,4:3999,]62:34:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-reset,20:2026-04-06T14:05:55Z,]46:32:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-limit,7:2400000,]50:36:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-remaining,7:2394000,]60:32:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T14:05:55Z,]46:10:request-id,28:req_011CZneQZzYUXrW9qyx4WpTL,]77:25:strict-transport-security,44:max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload,]69:25:anthropic-organization-id,36:19d39eaa-efb4-49e0-afe8-a7359703719a,]23:6:Server,10:cloudflare,]39:29:x-envoy-upstream-service-time,3:989,]27:16:Content-Encoding,4:gzip,]26:4:vary,15:Accept-Encoding,]45:13:server-timing,24:x-originResponse;dur=992,]29:15:cf-cache-status,7:DYNAMIC,]208:10:set-cookie,189:_cfuvid=4muYXkcv4EmQZFFbTxBWuEzjFPt5EKvUt7oqrlaT0wk-1775484355.7780888-1.0.1.1-SaV.qXVOfc.HH9yp2EoanJcjmZLBTbRr1VlPVruKYV0; HttpOnly; SameSite=None; Secure; Path=/; Domain=api.anthropic.com,]73:23:Content-Security-Policy,42:default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none',]23:12:X-Robots-Tag,4:none,]33:6:CF-RAY,20:9e8159a79d468063-DUB,]]12:http_version;8:HTTP/1.1,}7:request;110873:4:path;12:/v1/messages,9:authority;0:,6:scheme;5:https,6:method;4:POST,4:port;3:443#4:host;17:api.anthropic.com;13:timestamp_end;17:1775484355.663377^15:timestamp_start;18:1775484355.6622982^8:trailers;0:~7:content;110084:{"max_tokens":32768,"messages":[{"content":[{"text":"---\n## ⚡ Entering Phase: Execute\nYou are now in the **Execute** phase. Set aside any planning considerations or review feedback from previous phases — they no longer apply. Your only objective is defined below.\n---\n\nImplement the plan below precisely, file by file.\n\nThe Explore and Plan phases are complete. File contents read during those phases are available in the conversation history — check there before calling `read_file` to avoid reading the same file twice. If the content you need is not in the history, read it from disk using `read_file`.\n\nGuidelines:\n- Follow the plan exactly — do not add features, refactor unrelated code, or make unrequested improvements\n- Check conversation history for file content before calling `read_file`\n- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones\n- Do not add comments, docstrings, or type annotations to code you did not change\n- If you hit an unexpected blocker, stop and ask rather than working around it\n\n\u003cplan\u003e\n## Implementation Plan: French (fr) Language Support\n\n### Overview\n\nThe i18n system lives entirely in `/workspace/ui/src/i18n/`. Adding French requires changes to 5 existing files and 1 new file, following the exact patterns established by Spanish (`es.ts`) and Brazilian Portuguese (`pt-BR.ts`) as the most complete reference locales.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n**1. Create `/workspace/ui/src/i18n/locales/fr.ts`** (new file)\n\nExport a `fr` constant of type `TranslationMap`. Model it on `es.ts` (full cron section) and `pt-BR.ts` (has the extended tabs/subtitles keys added more recently). The file must cover every key present in `en.ts`:\n- `common` (health, ok, online, offline, connect, refresh, enabled, disabled, na, version, docs, theme, resources, search)\n- `nav` (chat, control, agent, settings, expand, collapse, resize)\n- `tabs` (all 18 keys including the newer ones: communications, appearance, automation, infrastructure, aiAgents)\n- `subtitles` (matching all tab keys)\n- `overview` (access, snapshot, stats, notes, auth, pairing, insecure, connection, cards, attention, eventLog, logTail, quickActions, palette)\n- `login` (subtitle, passwordPlaceholder)\n- `chat` (disconnected, refreshTitle, thinkingToggle, toolCallsToggle, focusToggle, hideCronSessions, showCronSessions, showCronSessionsHidden, onboardingDisabled)\n- `languages` (all 7 entries including the new `fr` key for French itself)\n- `cron` (summary, jobs, runs, form, jobList, jobDetail, jobState, runEntry, errors) - full section as in `es.ts`\n\nThe export name is `fr` (lowercase, matching the locale identifier, consistent with `de` and `es`).\n\n**2. Update `/workspace/ui/src/i18n/lib/types.ts`**\n\nChange the `Locale` type union from:\n```\nexport type Locale=\"en\"|\"zh-CN\"|\"zh-TW\"|\"pt-BR\"|\"de\"|\"es\";\n```\nto:\n```\nexport type Locale=\"en\"|\"zh-CN\"|\"zh-TW\"|\"pt-BR\"|\"de\"|\"es\"|\"fr\";\n```\n\n**3. Update `/workspace/ui/src/i18n/lib/registry.ts`**\n\nThree additions:\n\na) Add `\"fr\"` to `LAZY_LOCALES`:\n```\nconst LAZY_LOCALES:readonly LazyLocale[]=[\"zh-CN\",\"zh-TW\",\"pt-BR\",\"de\",\"es\",\"fr\"];\n```\n\nb) Add entry to `LAZY_LOCALE_REGISTRY`:\n```\nfr:{exportName:\"fr\",loader:()=\u003eimport(\"../locales/fr.ts\"),},\n```\n\nc) Add a `fr` branch in `resolveNavigatorLocale`:\n```\nif(navLang.startsWith(\"fr\")){return\"fr\";}\n```\nThis branch should appear before the final `return DEFAULT_LOCALE` fallback, consistent with how `de` and `es` are handled.\n\n**4. Update `/workspace/src/i18n/registry.test.ts`**\n\nThe test at line that reads:\n```\nexpect(SUPPORTED_LOCALES).toEqual([\"en\",\"zh-CN\",\"zh-TW\",\"pt-BR\",\"de\",\"es\"]);\n```\nmust be updated to:\n```\nexpect(SUPPORTED_LOCALES).toEqual([\"en\",\"zh-CN\",\"zh-TW\",\"pt-BR\",\"de\",\"es\",\"fr\"]);\n```\n\nAlso add a `resolveNavigatorLocale` assertion for French:\n```\nexpect(resolveNavigatorLocale(\"fr-FR\")).toBe(\"fr\");\n```\nin the \"resolves browser locale fallbacks\" test block alongside the existing `de-DE`, `es-ES`, etc. assertions.\n\nAlso add a lazy locale load assertion for French in \"loads lazy locale translations from the registry\":\n```\nconst fr=await loadLazyLocaleTranslation(\"fr\");\nexpect(getNestedTranslation(fr,\"common\",\"health\")).toBe(\"Santé\");\n```\n\n**5. Update all existing locale files to add `fr` to their `languages` section**\n\nEach existing non-English locale file has a `languages` block listing all supported languages. All 5 need a new `fr` entry:\n\n- `/workspace/ui/src/i18n/locales/de.ts`: Add `fr:\"Französisch (French)\"` (or `fr:\"Französisch\"`)\n- `/workspace/ui/src/i18n/locales/es.ts`: Add `fr:\"Francés (French)\"` (or `fr:\"Francés\"`)\n- `/workspace/ui/src/i18n/locales/pt-BR.ts`: Add `fr:\"Français (Francês)\"` (or `fr:\"Francês (Français)\"`)\n- `/workspace/ui/src/i18n/locales/zh-CN.ts`: Add `fr:\"Français (法语)\"` (or `fr:\"法语 (Français)\"`)\n- `/workspace/ui/src/i18n/locales/zh-TW.ts`: Add `fr:\"Français (法語)\"` (or `fr:\"法語 (Français)\"`)\n- `/workspace/ui/src/i18n/locales/en.ts`: Add `fr:\"Français (French)\"` to the `languages` section\n\n**6. Create a git branch**\n\nBefore implementing, create a new branch from the current HEAD:\n```\ngit checkout -b feat/fr-i18n\n```\nThis produces a PR-ready branch named `feat/fr-i18n`.\n\n### Translation Content for `fr.ts`\n\nKey French translations to use (professional/formal register, consistent with other locales):\n\n- `common.health` = `\"Santé\"` (this is what the test will assert)\n- `common.ok` = `\"OK\"`\n- `common.online` = `\"En ligne\"`\n- `common.offline` = `\"Hors ligne\"`\n- `common.connect` = `\"Connecter\"`\n- `common.refresh` = `\"Actualiser\"`\n- `common.enabled` = `\"Activé\"`\n- `common.disabled` = `\"Désactivé\"`\n- `common.na` = `\"n/d\"` (non disponible, or `\"n/a\"` is also acceptable)\n- `common.version` = `\"Version\"`\n- `common.docs` = `\"Documentation\"`\n- `common.theme` = `\"Thème\"`\n- `common.resources` = `\"Ressources\"`\n- `common.search` = `\"Rechercher\"`\n- `nav.settings` = `\"Paramètres\"`\n- `overview.access.title` = `\"Accès à la passerelle\"`\n- `overview.access.language` = `\"Langue\"`\n- `languages.fr` = `\"Français\"` (self-reference, no parenthetical needed)\n- `languages.en` = `\"Anglais (English)\"`\n- `languages.de` = `\"Deutsch (Allemand)\"`\n- `languages.es` = `\"Español (Espagnol)\"`\n- `languages.ptBR` = `\"Português (Portugais brésilien)\"`\n- `languages.zhCN` = `\"简体中文 (Chinois simplifié)\"`\n- `languages.zhTW` = `\"繁體中文 (Chinois traditionnel)\"`\n\n### Sequencing\n\n1. Create branch\n2. Create `fr.ts` (largest single change, no dependencies)\n3. Update `types.ts` (simple union addition, needed for TypeScript to accept `\"fr\"` as a `Locale`)\n4. Update `registry.ts` (depends on `types.ts` compiling cleanly)\n5. Update `en.ts` and the 5 other locale files to add `fr` to their `languages` section\n6. Update `registry.test.ts` to include `fr` in all relevant assertions\n\n### Potential Challenges\n\n- The `SUPPORTED_LOCALES` test is an exact `.toEqual()` match on an ordered array. The order matters: `\"fr\"` must be appended at the end, after `\"es\"`.\n- `pt-BR.ts` has more keys than `de.ts` or `es.ts` (it includes `toolCallsToggle` in chat and the full connection/cards/attention/eventLog/logTail/quickActions/palette subsections). The `fr.ts` file should match the most complete locale (`en.ts`) to avoid silent fallbacks.\n- `en.ts` also has `common.theme` and `nav.resize` and `tabs.communications/appearance/automation/infrastructure/aiAgents` which some older locale files are missing. The `fr.ts` should include all of these.\n\n### Critical Files for Implementation\n\n- `/workspace/ui/src/i18n/locales/fr.ts` - New French translation file to create (largest change)\n- `/workspace/ui/src/i18n/lib/types.ts` - Add `\"fr\"` to the `Locale` union type\n- `/workspace/ui/src/i18n/lib/registry.ts` - Register `fr` in lazy loaders and navigator resolution\n- `/workspace/src/i18n/registry.test.ts` - Update test assertions to include `fr`\n- `/workspace/ui/src/i18n/locales/en.ts` - Add `fr` entry to `languages` section (pattern to follow for all other locale files)\n\u003c/plan\u003e","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[{"text":"I'll implement the French (fr) language support. Let me start by reading the necessary files to understand the current state.","type":"text"},{"id":"toolu_01RmwV6dUxCjdWAHLuQV1uVF","input":{"path":"/workspace/ui/src/i18n/locales/en.ts","reason":"Need to see all keys to implement fr.ts completely"},"name":"read_file","type":"tool_use"},{"id":"toolu_01DTMw22X3ry64F1GJPpsVhn","input":{"path":"/workspace/ui/src/i18n/locales/es.ts","reason":"Reference for full cron section and structure"},"name":"read_file","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},{"content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RmwV6dUxCjdWAHLuQV1uVF","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"    1\timport type { TranslationMap } from \"../lib/types.ts\";\n    2\t\n    3\texport const en: TranslationMap = {\n    4\t  common: {\n    5\t    health: \"Health\",\n    6\t    ok: \"OK\",\n    7\t    online: \"Online\",\n    8\t    offline: \"Offline\",\n    9\t    connect: \"Connect\",\n   10\t    refresh: \"Refresh\",\n   11\t    enabled: \"Enabled\",\n   12\t    disabled: \"Disabled\",\n   13\t    na: \"n/a\",\n   14\t    version: \"Version\",\n   15\t    docs: \"Docs\",\n   16\t    theme: \"Theme\",\n   17\t    resources: \"Resources\",\n   18\t    search: \"Search\",\n   19\t  },\n   20\t  nav: {\n   21\t    chat: \"Chat\",\n   22\t    control: \"Control\",\n   23\t    agent: \"Agent\",\n   24\t    settings: \"Settings\",\n   25\t    expand: \"Expand sidebar\",\n   26\t    collapse: \"Collapse sidebar\",\n   27\t    resize: \"Resize sidebar\",\n   28\t  },\n   29\t  tabs: {\n   30\t    agents: \"Agents\",\n   31\t    overview: \"Overview\",\n   32\t    channels: \"Channels\",\n   33\t    instances: \"Instances\",\n   34\t    sessions: \"Sessions\",\n   35\t    usage: \"Usage\",\n   36\t    cron: \"Cron Jobs\",\n   37\t    skills: \"Skills\",\n   38\t    nodes: \"Nodes\",\n   39\t    chat: \"Chat\",\n   40\t    config: \"Config\",\n   41\t    communications: \"Communications\",\n   42\t    appearance: \"Appearance\",\n   43\t    automation: \"Automation\",\n   44\t    infrastructure: \"Infrastructure\",\n   45\t    aiAgents: \"AI \u0026 Agents\",\n   46\t    debug: \"Debug\",\n   47\t    logs: \"Logs\",\n   48\t  },\n   49\t  subtitles: {\n   50\t    agents: \"Workspaces, tools, identities.\",\n   51\t    overview: \"Status, entry points, health.\",\n   52\t    channels: \"Channels and settings.\",\n   53\t    instances: \"Connected clients and nodes.\",\n   54\t    sessions: \"Active sessions and defaults.\",\n   55\t    usage: \"API usage and costs.\",\n   56\t    cron: \"Wakeups and recurring runs.\",\n   57\t    skills: \"Skills and API keys.\",\n   58\t    nodes: \"Paired devices and commands.\",\n   59\t    chat: \"Gateway chat for quick interventions.\",\n   60\t    config: \"Edit openclaw.json.\",\n   61\t    communications: \"Channels, messages, and audio settings.\",\n   62\t    appearance: \"Theme, UI, and setup wizard settings.\",\n   63\t    automation: \"Commands, hooks, cron, and plugins.\",\n   64\t    infrastructure: \"Gateway, web, browser, and media settings.\",\n   65\t    aiAgents: \"Agents, models, skills, tools, memory, session.\",\n   66\t    debug: \"Snapshots, events, RPC.\",\n   67\t    logs: \"Live gateway logs.\",\n   68\t  },\n   69\t  overview: {\n   70\t    access: {\n   71\t      title: \"Gateway Access\",\n   72\t      subtitle: \"Where the dashboard connects and how it authenticates.\",\n   73\t      wsUrl: \"WebSocket URL\",\n   74\t      token: \"Gateway Token\",\n   75\t      password: \"Password (not stored)\",\n   76\t      sessionKey: \"Default Session Key\",\n   77\t      language: \"Language\",\n   78\t      connectHint: \"Click Connect to apply connection changes.\",\n   79\t      trustedProxy: \"Authenticated via trusted proxy.\",\n   80\t    },\n   81\t    snapshot: {\n   82\t      title: \"Snapshot\",\n   83\t      subtitle: \"Latest gateway handshake information.\",\n   84\t      status: \"Status\",\n   85\t      uptime: \"Uptime\",\n   86\t      tickInterval: \"Tick Interval\",\n   87\t      lastChannelsRefresh: \"Last Channels Refresh\",\n   88\t      channelsHint: \"Use Channels to link WhatsApp, Telegram, Discord, Signal, or iMessage.\",\n   89\t    },\n   90\t    stats: {\n   91\t      instances: \"Instances\",\n   92\t      instancesHint: \"Presence beacons in the last 5 minutes.\",\n   93\t      sessions: \"Sessions\",\n   94\t      sessionsHint: \"Recent session keys tracked by the gateway.\",\n   95\t      cron: \"Cron\",\n   96\t      cronNext: \"Next wake {time}\",\n   97\t    },\n   98\t    notes: {\n   99\t      title: \"Notes\",\n  100\t      subtitle: \"Quick reminders for remote control setups.\",\n  101\t      tailscaleTitle: \"Tailscale serve\",\n  102\t      tailscaleText: \"Prefer serve mode to keep the gateway on loopback with tailnet auth.\",\n  103\t      sessionTitle: \"Session hygiene\",\n  104\t      sessionText: \"Use /new or sessions.patch to reset context.\",\n  105\t      cronTitle: \"Cron reminders\",\n  106\t      cronText: \"Use isolated sessions for recurring runs.\",\n  107\t    },\n  108\t    auth: {\n  109\t      required: \"This gateway requires auth. Add a token or password, then click Connect.\",\n  110\t      failed:\n  111\t        \"Auth failed. Re-copy a tokenized URL with {command}, or update the token, then click Connect.\",\n  112\t    },\n  113\t    pairing: {\n  114\t      hint: \"This device needs pairing approval from the gateway host.\",\n  115\t      mobileHint:\n  116\t        \"On mobile? Copy the full URL (including #token=...) from openclaw dashboard --no-open on your desktop.\",\n  117\t    },\n  118\t    insecure: {\n  119\t      hint: \"This page is HTTP, so the browser blocks device identity. Use HTTPS (Tailscale Serve) or open {url} on the gateway host.\",\n  120\t      stayHttp: \"If you must stay on HTTP, set {config} (token-only).\",\n  121\t    },\n  122\t    connection: {\n  123\t      title: \"How to connect\",\n  124\t      step1: \"Start the gateway on your host machine:\",\n  125\t      step2: \"Get a tokenized dashboard URL:\",\n  126\t      step3: \"Paste the WebSocket URL and token above, or open the tokenized URL directly.\",\n  127\t      step4: \"Or generate a reusable token:\",\n  128\t      docsHint: \"For remote access, Tailscale Serve is recommended. \",\n  129\t      docsLink: \"Read the docs →\",\n  130\t    },\n  131\t    cards: {\n  132\t      cost: \"Cost\",\n  133\t      skills: \"Skills\",\n  134\t      recentSessions: \"Recent Sessions\",\n  135\t    },\n  136\t    attention: {\n  137\t      title: \"Attention\",\n  138\t    },\n  139\t    eventLog: {\n  140\t      title: \"Event Log\",\n  141\t    },\n  142\t    logTail: {\n  143\t      title: \"Gateway Logs\",\n  144\t    },\n  145\t    quickActions: {\n  146\t      newSession: \"New Session\",\n  147\t      automation: \"Automation\",\n  148\t      refreshAll: \"Refresh All\",\n  149\t      terminal: \"Terminal\",\n  150\t    },\n  151\t    palette: {\n  152\t      placeholder: \"Type a command…\",\n  153\t      noResults: \"No results\",\n  154\t    },\n  155\t  },\n  156\t  login: {\n  157\t    subtitle: \"Gateway Dashboard\",\n  158\t    passwordPlaceholder: \"optional\",\n  159\t  },\n  160\t  chat: {\n  161\t    disconnected: \"Disconnected from gateway.\",\n  162\t    refreshTitle: \"Refresh chat data\",\n  163\t    thinkingToggle: \"Toggle assistant thinking/working output\",\n  164\t    toolCallsToggle: \"Toggle tool calls and tool results\",\n  165\t    focusToggle: \"Toggle focus mode (hide sidebar + page header)\",\n  166\t    hideCronSessions: \"Hide cron sessions\",\n  167\t    showCronSessions: \"Show cron sessions\",\n  168\t    showCronSessionsHidden: \"Show cron sessions ({count} hidden)\",\n  169\t    onboardingDisabled: \"Disabled during setup\",\n  170\t  },\n  171\t  languages: {\n  172\t    en: \"English\",\n  173\t    zhCN: \"简体中文 (Simplified Chinese)\",\n  174\t    zhTW: \"繁體中文 (Traditional Chinese)\",\n  175\t    ptBR: \"Português (Brazilian Portuguese)\",\n  176\t    de: \"Deutsch (German)\",\n  177\t    es: \"Español (Spanish)\",\n  178\t  },\n  179\t  cron: {\n  180\t    summary: {\n  181\t      enabled: \"Enabled\",\n  182\t      yes: \"Yes\",\n  183\t      no: \"No\",\n  184\t      jobs: \"Jobs\",\n  185\t      nextWake: \"Next wake\",\n  186\t      refreshing: \"Refreshing...\",\n  187\t      refresh: \"Refresh\",\n  188\t    },\n  189\t    jobs: {\n  190\t      title: \"Jobs\",\n  191\t      subtitle: \"All scheduled jobs stored in the gateway.\",\n  192\t      shownOf: \"{shown} shown of {total}\",\n  193\t      searchJobs: \"Search jobs\",\n  194\t      searchPlaceholder: \"Name, description, or agent\",\n  195\t      enabled: \"Enabled\",\n  196\t      schedule: \"Schedule\",\n  197\t      lastRun: \"Last run\",\n  198\t      all: \"All\",\n  199\t      sort: \"Sort\",\n  200\t      nextRun: \"Next run\",\n  201\t      recentlyUpdated: \"Recently updated\",\n  202\t      name: \"Name\",\n  203\t      direction: \"Direction\",\n  204\t      ascending: \"Ascending\",\n  205\t      descending: \"Descending\",\n  206\t      reset: \"Reset\",\n  207\t      noMatching: \"No matching jobs.\",\n  208\t      loading: \"Loading...\",\n  209\t      loadMore: \"Load more jobs\",\n  210\t    },\n  211\t    runs: {\n  212\t      title: \"Run history\",\n  213\t      subtitleAll: \"Latest runs across all jobs.\",\n  214\t      subtitleJob: \"Latest runs for {title}.\",\n  215\t      scope: \"Scope\",\n  216\t      allJobs: \"All jobs\",\n  217\t      selectedJob: \"Selected job\",\n  218\t      searchRuns: \"Search runs\",\n  219\t      searchPlaceholder: \"Summary, error, or job\",\n  220\t      newestFirst: \"Newest first\",\n  221\t      oldestFirst: \"Oldest first\",\n  222\t      status: \"Status\",\n  223\t      delivery: \"Delivery\",\n  224\t      clear: \"Clear\",\n  225\t      allStatuses: \"All statuses\",\n  226\t      allDelivery: \"All delivery\",\n  227\t      selectJobHint: \"Select a job to inspect run history.\",\n  228\t      noMatching: \"No matching runs.\",\n  229\t      loadMore: \"Load more runs\",\n  230\t      runStatusOk: \"OK\",\n  231\t      runStatusError: \"Error\",\n  232\t      runStatusSkipped: \"Skipped\",\n  233\t      runStatusUnknown: \"Unknown\",\n  234\t      deliveryDelivered: \"Delivered\",\n  235\t      deliveryNotDelivered: \"Not delivered\",\n  236\t      deliveryUnknown: \"Unknown\",\n  237\t      deliveryNotRequested: \"Not requested\",\n  238\t    },\n  239\t    form: {\n  240\t      editJob: \"Edit Job\",\n  241\t      newJob: \"New Job\",\n  242\t      updateSubtitle: \"Update the selected scheduled job.\",\n  243\t      createSubtitle: \"Create a scheduled wakeup or agent run.\",\n  244\t      required: \"Required\",\n  245\t      requiredSr: \"required\",\n  246\t      basics: \"Basics\",\n  247\t      basicsSub: \"Name it, choose the assistant, and set enabled state.\",\n  248\t      fieldName: \"Name\",\n  249\t      description: \"Description\",\n  250\t      agentId: \"Agent ID\",\n  251\t      namePlaceholder: \"Morning brief\",\n  252\t      descriptionPlaceholder: \"Optional context for this job\",\n  253\t      agentPlaceholder: \"main or ops\",\n  254\t      agentHelp: \"Start typing to pick a known agent, or enter a custom one.\",\n  255\t      schedule: \"Schedule\",\n  256\t      scheduleSub: \"Control when this job runs.\",\n  257\t      every: \"Every\",\n  258\t      at: \"At\",\n  259\t      cronOption: \"Cron\",\n  260\t      runAt: \"Run at\",\n  261\t      unit: \"Unit\",\n  262\t      minutes: \"Minutes\",\n  263\t      hours: \"Hours\",\n  264\t      days: \"Days\",\n  265\t      expression: \"Expression\",\n  266\t      expressionPlaceholder: \"0 7 * * *\",\n  267\t      everyAmountPlaceholder: \"30\",\n  268\t      timezoneOptional: \"Timezone (optional)\",\n  269\t      timezonePlaceholder: \"America/Los_Angeles\",\n  270\t      timezoneHelp: \"Pick a common timezone or enter any valid IANA timezone.\",\n  271\t      jitterHelp: \"Need jitter? Use Advanced → Stagger window / Stagger unit.\",\n  272\t      execution: \"Execution\",\n  273\t      executionSub: \"Choose when to wake, and what this job should do.\",\n  274\t      session: \"Session\",\n  275\t      main: \"Main\",\n  276\t      isolated: \"Isolated\",\n  277\t      sessionHelp: \"Main posts a system event. Isolated runs a dedicated agent turn.\",\n  278\t      wakeMode: \"Wake mode\",\n  279\t      now: \"Now\",\n  280\t      nextHeartbeat: \"Next heartbeat\",\n  281\t      wakeModeHelp: \"Now triggers immediately. Next heartbeat waits for the next cycle.\",\n  282\t      payloadKind: \"What should run?\",\n  283\t      systemEvent: \"Post message to main timeline\",\n  284\t      agentTurn: \"Run assistant task (isolated)\",\n  285\t      systemEventHelp:\n  286\t        \"Sends your text to the gateway main timeline (good for reminders/triggers).\",\n  287\t      agentTurnHelp: \"Starts an assistant run in its own session using your prompt.\",\n  288\t      timeoutSeconds: \"Timeout (seconds)\",\n  289\t      timeoutPlaceholder: \"Optional, e.g. 90\",\n  290\t      timeoutHelp:\n  291\t        \"Optional. Leave blank to use the gateway default timeout behavior for this run.\",\n  292\t      mainTimelineMessage: \"Main timeline message\",\n  293\t      assistantTaskPrompt: \"Assistant task prompt\",\n  294\t      deliverySection: \"Delivery\",\n  295\t      deliverySub: \"Choose where run summaries are sent.\",\n  296\t      resultDelivery: \"Result delivery\",\n  297\t      announceDefault: \"Announce summary (default)\",\n  298\t      webhookPost: \"Webhook POST\",\n  299\t      noneInternal: \"None (internal)\",\n  300\t      deliveryHelp: \"Announce posts a summary to chat. None keeps execution internal.\",\n  301\t      webhookUrl: \"Webhook URL\",\n  302\t      channel: \"Channel\",\n  303\t      webhookPlaceholder: \"https://example.com/cron\",\n  304\t      channelHelp: \"Choose which connected channel receives the summary.\",\n  305\t      webhookHelp: \"Send run summaries to a webhook endpoint.\",\n  306\t      to: \"To\",\n  307\t      toPlaceholder: \"+1555... or chat id\",\n  308\t      toHelp: \"Optional recipient override (chat id, phone, or user id).\",\n  309\t      advanced: \"Advanced\",\n  310\t      advancedHelp:\n  311\t        \"Optional overrides for delivery guarantees, schedule jitter, and model controls.\",\n  312\t      deleteAfterRun: \"Delete after run\",\n  313\t      deleteAfterRunHelp: \"Best for one-shot reminders that should auto-clean up.\",\n  314\t      clearAgentOverride: \"Clear agent override\",\n  315\t      clearAgentHelp: \"Force this job to use the gateway default assistant.\",\n  316\t      exactTiming: \"Exact timing (no stagger)\",\n  317\t      exactTimingHelp: \"Run on exact cron boundaries with no spread.\",\n  318\t      staggerWindow: \"Stagger window\",\n  319\t      staggerUnit: \"Stagger unit\",\n  320\t      staggerPlaceholder: \"30\",\n  321\t      seconds: \"Seconds\",\n  322\t      model: \"Model\",\n  323\t      modelPlaceholder: \"openai/gpt-5.2\",\n  324\t      modelHelp: \"Start typing to pick a known model, or enter a custom one.\",\n  325\t      thinking: \"Thinking\",\n  326\t      thinkingPlaceholder: \"low\",\n  327\t      thinkingHelp: \"Use a suggested level or enter a provider-specific value.\",\n  328\t      bestEffortDelivery: \"Best effort delivery\",\n  329\t      bestEffortHelp: \"Do not fail the job if delivery itself fails.\",\n  330\t      cantAddYet: \"Can't add job yet\",\n  331\t      fillRequired: \"Fill the required fields below to enable submit.\",\n  332\t      fixFields: \"Fix {count} field to continue.\",\n  333\t      fixFieldsPlural: \"Fix {count} fields to continue.\",\n  334\t      saving: \"Saving...\",\n  335\t      saveChanges: \"Save changes\",\n  336\t      addJob: \"Add job\",\n  337\t      cancel: \"Cancel\",\n  338\t    },\n  339\t    jobList: {\n  340\t      allJobs: \"all jobs\",\n  341\t      selectJob: \"(select a job)\",\n  342\t      enabled: \"enabled\",\n  343\t      disabled: \"disabled\",\n  344\t      edit: \"Edit\",\n  345\t      clone: \"Clone\",\n  346\t      disable: \"Disable\",\n  347\t      enable: \"Enable\",\n  348\t      run: \"Run\",\n  349\t      history: \"History\",\n  350\t      remove: \"Remove\",\n  351\t    },\n  352\t    jobDetail: {\n  353\t      system: \"System\",\n  354\t      prompt: \"Prompt\",\n  355\t      delivery: \"Delivery\",\n  356\t      agent: \"Agent\",\n  357\t    },\n  358\t    jobState: {\n  359\t      status: \"Status\",\n  360\t      next: \"Next\",\n  361\t      last: \"Last\",\n  362\t    },\n  363\t    runEntry: {\n  364\t      noSummary: \"No summary.\",\n  365\t      runAt: \"Run at\",\n  366\t      openRunChat: \"Open run chat\",\n  367\t      next: \"Next {rel}\",\n  368\t      due: \"Due {rel}\",\n  369\t    },\n  370\t    errors: {\n  371\t      nameRequired: \"Name is required.\",\n  372\t      scheduleAtInvalid: \"Enter a valid date/time.\",\n  373\t      everyAmountInvalid: \"Interval must be greater than 0.\",\n  374\t      cronExprRequired: \"Cron expression is required.\",\n  375\t      staggerAmountInvalid: \"Stagger must be greater than 0.\",\n  376\t      systemTextRequired: \"System text is required.\",\n  377\t      agentMessageRequired: \"Agent message is required.\",\n  378\t      timeoutInvalid: \"If set, timeout must be greater than 0 seconds.\",\n  379\t      webhookUrlRequired: \"Webhook URL is required.\",\n  380\t      webhookUrlInvalid: \"Webhook URL must start with http:// or https://.\",\n  381\t      invalidRunTime: \"Invalid run time.\",\n  382\t      invalidIntervalAmount: \"Invalid interval amount.\",\n  383\t      cronExprRequiredShort: \"Cron expression required.\",\n  384\t      invalidStaggerAmount: \"Invalid stagger amount.\",\n  385\t      systemEventTextRequired: \"System event text required.\",\n  386\t      agentMessageRequiredShort: \"Agent message required.\",\n  387\t      nameRequiredShort: \"Name required.\",\n  388\t    },\n  389\t  },\n  390\t};\n  391\t","type":"text"}],"type":"tool_result"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DTMw22X3ry64F1GJPpsVhn","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"    1\timport type { TranslationMap } from \"../lib/types.ts\";\n    2\t\n    3\texport const es: TranslationMap = {\n    4\t  common: {\n    5\t    version: \"Versión\",\n    6\t    health: \"Estado\",\n    7\t    ok: \"Correcto\",\n    8\t    online: \"En línea\",\n    9\t    offline: \"Desconectado\",\n   10\t    connect: \"Conectar\",\n   11\t    refresh: \"Actualizar\",\n   12\t    enabled: \"Habilitado\",\n   13\t    disabled: \"Deshabilitado\",\n   14\t    na: \"n/a\",\n   15\t    docs: \"Docs\",\n   16\t    resources: \"Recursos\",\n   17\t  },\n   18\t  nav: {\n   19\t    chat: \"Chat\",\n   20\t    control: \"Control\",\n   21\t    agent: \"Agente\",\n   22\t    settings: \"Ajustes\",\n   23\t    expand: \"Expandir barra lateral\",\n   24\t    collapse: \"Contraer barra lateral\",\n   25\t  },\n   26\t  tabs: {\n   27\t    agents: \"Agentes\",\n   28\t    overview: \"Resumen\",\n   29\t    channels: \"Canales\",\n   30\t    instances: \"Instancias\",\n   31\t    sessions: \"Sesiones\",\n   32\t    usage: \"Uso\",\n   33\t    cron: \"Tareas Cron\",\n   34\t    skills: \"Habilidades\",\n   35\t    nodes: \"Nodos\",\n   36\t    chat: \"Chat\",\n   37\t    config: \"Configuración\",\n   38\t    debug: \"Depuración\",\n   39\t    logs: \"Registros\",\n   40\t  },\n   41\t  subtitles: {\n   42\t    agents: \"Gestionar espacios de trabajo, herramientas e identidades de agentes.\",\n   43\t    overview: \"Estado de la puerta de enlace, puntos de entrada y lectura rápida de salud.\",\n   44\t    channels: \"Gestionar canales y ajustes.\",\n   45\t    instances: \"Balizas de presencia de clientes y nodos conectados.\",\n   46\t    sessions: \"Inspeccionar sesiones activas y ajustar valores predeterminados por sesión.\",\n   47\t    usage: \"Monitorear uso de API y costes.\",\n   48\t    cron: \"Programar despertares y ejecuciones recurrentes de agentes.\",\n   49\t    skills: \"Gestionar disponibilidad de habilidades e inyección de claves API.\",\n   50\t    nodes: \"Dispositivos emparejados, capacidades y exposición de comandos.\",\n   51\t    chat: \"Sesión de chat directa con la puerta de enlace para intervenciones rápidas.\",\n   52\t    config: \"Editar ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json de forma segura.\",\n   53\t    debug: \"Instantáneas de la puerta de enlace, eventos y llamadas RPC manuales.\",\n   54\t    logs: \"Seguimiento en vivo de los registros de la puerta de enlace.\",\n   55\t  },\n   56\t  overview: {\n   57\t    access: {\n   58\t      title: \"Acceso a la puerta de enlace\",\n   59\t      subtitle: \"Dónde se conecta el panel y cómo se autentica.\",\n   60\t      wsUrl: \"URL de WebSocket\",\n   61\t      token: \"Token de la puerta de enlace\",\n   62\t      password: \"Contraseña (no se guarda)\", // pragma: allowlist secret\n   63\t      sessionKey: \"Clave de sesión predeterminada\",\n   64\t      language: \"Idioma\",\n   65\t      connectHint: \"Haz clic en Conectar para aplicar los cambios de conexión.\",\n   66\t      trustedProxy: \"Autenticado mediante proxy de confianza.\",\n   67\t    },\n   68\t    snapshot: {\n   69\t      title: \"Instantánea\",\n   70\t      subtitle: \"Información más reciente del saludo con la puerta de enlace.\",\n   71\t      status: \"Estado\",\n   72\t      uptime: \"Tiempo de actividad\",\n   73\t      tickInterval: \"Intervalo de tick\",\n   74\t      lastChannelsRefresh: \"Última actualización de canales\",\n   75\t      channelsHint: \"Usa Canales para vincular WhatsApp, Telegram, Discord, Signal o iMessage.\",\n   76\t    },\n   77\t    stats: {\n   78\t      instances: \"Instancias\",\n   79\t      instancesHint: \"Balizas de presencia en los últimos 5 minutos.\",\n   80\t      sessions: \"Sesiones\",\n   81\t      sessionsHint: \"Claves de sesión recientes rastreadas por la puerta de enlace.\",\n   82\t      cron: \"Cron\",\n   83\t      cronNext: \"Próximo despertar {time}\",\n   84\t    },\n   85\t    notes: {\n   86\t      title: \"Notas\",\n   87\t      subtitle: \"Recordatorios rápidos para configuraciones de control remoto.\",\n   88\t      tailscaleTitle: \"Tailscale serve\",\n   89\t      tailscaleText:\n   90\t        \"Prefiere el modo serve para mantener la puerta de enlace en loopback con autenticación tailnet.\",\n   91\t      sessionTitle: \"Higiene de sesión\",\n   92\t      sessionText: \"Usa /new o sessions.patch para reiniciar el contexto.\",\n   93\t      cronTitle: \"Recordatorios de Cron\",\n   94\t      cronText: \"Usa sesiones aisladas para ejecuciones recurrentes.\",\n   95\t    },\n   96\t    auth: {\n   97\t      required:\n   98\t        \"Esta puerta de enlace requiere autenticación. Añade un token o contraseña y haz clic en Conectar.\",\n   99\t      failed:\n  100\t        \"Autenticación fallida. Vuelve a copiar una URL con token mediante {command}, o actualiza el token y haz clic en Conectar.\",\n  101\t    },\n  102\t    pairing: {\n  103\t      hint: \"Este dispositivo necesita aprobación de emparejamiento del host de la puerta de enlace.\",\n  104\t      mobileHint:\n  105\t        \"¿En el móvil? Copia la URL completa (incluyendo #token=...) desde openclaw dashboard --no-open en tu escritorio.\",\n  106\t    },\n  107\t    insecure: {\n  108\t      hint: \"Esta página es HTTP, p